.TH CISS 1 "2026-08-04" "CISS" "Croft Item Storage Server"
.SH NAME
ciss \- Croft Item Storage Server: a metered, PDS-like object store
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ciss
.B \-\-data\-dir
.I path
.B \-\-listen
.I host:port
.br
.B ciss usage
.B \-\-data\-dir
.I path
.RB [ \-\-did
.IR did ]
.br
.B ciss \-\-help
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B ciss
is a cooperative metered\-storage server. It exposes an S3\-compatible object
interface and an atproto PDS blob API over one metered byte\-path: every byte that
crosses the boundary is metered with a provider\-signed receipt, and rent is
derived from the customer's own signed manifest.
.PP
The bare invocation runs the server. The
.B usage
subcommand is a read\-only operator report over the same data directory.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B (server)
Run the metered\-storage server. Binds a loopback port (TLS is terminated by the
front proxy) and self\-manages its layout under
.IR \-\-data\-dir .
.TP
.B usage
Print a storage\-usage report: the whole\-store distinct\-bytes ceiling and its
percentage of the partition the data dir is on, and, per DID, on\-disk stored bytes
alongside cumulative transferred bytes. Opens the live database
.B read\-only
(safe while the service is running). With
.B \-\-did
it reports a single DID.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-data\-dir " path"
State directory. Holds
.IR meter.sqlite " (the per\-DID metering ledger and the provider public key),"
.IR blocks/ " (content\-addressed blobs), and " tmp/ " (write staging)."
Default:
.IR ./data .
.TP
.BI \-\-listen " host:port"
Loopback bind address for the server. Default:
.IR 127.0.0.1:8080 .
.TP
.BI \-\-did " did"
.RB ( usage
only) report a single DID instead of all DIDs.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show help (top\-level, or for the
.B usage
subcommand).
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B CISS_PROVIDER_SEED
The provider signing seed (hex). In production this is supplied as a systemd
encrypted credential at
.IR $CREDENTIALS_DIRECTORY/provider\-seed ;
the seed is never stored in the database. Under systemd, if neither the
credential nor this variable is present, the service
.B fails closed.
.TP
.B CISS_MAX_STORE_BYTES
The whole\-store distinct\-bytes ceiling, always enforced. A new store that would
exceed it is refused with
.BR "507 Insufficient Storage" .
Default: 50 GiB.
.TP
.B CISS_MAX_DID_BYTES
An optional per\-DID distinct\-bytes cap. If unset (or 0), DIDs fill the store
opportunistically up to the whole\-store ceiling. If set, a DID's new store past
the cap is refused with
.BR 507 .
.TP
.B CISS_SERVICE_DID
This service's atproto DID \(em the
.I aud
a service\-auth JWT must name. Also the document served at
.IR /.well-known/did.json .
Default:
.IR did:web:ciss.croft.ing .
.TP
.B CISS_PLC_DIRECTORY_URL
The
.I did:plc
directory base URL for DID resolution. Default:
.IR https://plc.directory .
.TP
.B CISS_DID_RESOLVE_TIMEOUT_MS
Hard timeout for a DID resolution (milliseconds). An overrun fails closed.
Default: 3000.
.TP
.B CISS_DID_CACHE_TTL_S
TTL for the DID\-resolution cache (seconds). Default: 300.
.TP
.B CISS_ADMIN_PINS_FILE
Optional path to a pinned\-admin\-DID file: non\-empty, non\-`#` lines of
.IR "<did> <did:key>" .
Pinned DIDs resolve locally, never via the network (poisoning\-resistant
break\-glass). A malformed file fails startup loudly.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I <data-dir>/meter.sqlite
The canonical metering ledger and the durable provider public key. Exposes a
.B did_usage
view (the stable, read\-only usage API that
.B ciss usage
consumes).
.TP
.I <data-dir>/blocks/{did}/{cid}
Content\-addressed blob bytes.
.SH EXAMPLES
Run the server:
.PP
.RS
.EX
ciss \-\-data\-dir /var/lib/ciss \-\-listen 127.0.0.1:8301
.EE
.RE
.PP
Report storage usage for all DIDs, then one DID:
.PP
.RS
.EX
ciss usage \-\-data\-dir /var/lib/ciss
ciss usage \-\-data\-dir /var/lib/ciss \-\-did id:me
.EE
.RE
.SH SECURITY
See
.I docs/SECURITY\-POSTURE.md
in the source tree for the trust model and the security invariants (the design
reference for audits).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR systemd\-creds (1),
.BR statvfs (3)
